TY  - JOUR
T1  - Clinical trials to gain FDA approval for computerized cognitive training: What is the ideal control condition?
AN  - 1847423224; 2016-56491-001
AB  - This article briefs the ideal control conditions to gain Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approval for computerized cognitive training. The explosive growth of mobile technologies combined with the rapid rise of aging populations fearful of their risk for Alzheimer’s disease has led to a number of marketed products aimed at enhancing cognitive health. These include participant expectancy, engagement, motivation, novelty, and therapist interaction. We herein discuss the types of non-specific factors, desirable qualities of an active control condition, and the nuances that exist between previously used control conditions within the context of CCT for mild cognitive impairment. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
