TY  - JOUR
T1  - Plasticity of cognitive functions in elderly with subjective memory complaints: A review
AN  - 1905877484; 2016-42859-008
AB  - The progression of Alzheimer's disease (AD) might begin decades before onset of clinical symptoms, it would be more appropriate to prevent or postpone the disease process by intervening in this earlier stage of subjective memory complaints (SMC). The elderly with SMC demonstrate some neurodegenerative brain changes and have high risk of developing dementia, while relatively little is known about the effectiveness of cognitive training for SMC. Most of the existing few training studies target on the SMC were designed not rigorous, and the indicators for training effect were not comprehensive. Therefore, further research is necessary to discuss the influence of cognitive training on cognitive functions for SMC. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
 (Source: journal abstract)
