TY  - JOUR
T1  - A novel modification of the “method of loci” to improve memory in older adults
AN  - 1773463430; 2015-55466-005
AB  - A novel modification used in this pilot study adds elements of movement and music to the traditional method of loci. The goal of the study was to examine if this modified method improves memory function. Research participants were regular attendees of an adult day care center. Cognitive function was evaluated at baseline and following five months of training with a set of computerized neurocognitive tests tapping multiple domains. Significant improvement was found in memory function. This method combines pleasurable physical and social activities along with a cognitive training technique to improve memory in older adults. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2024 APA, all rights reserved)
