TY  - JOUR
T1  - The effect of art therapy on cognitive performance among ethnically diverse older adults
AN  - 1501842371; 2013-43417-005
AB  - This study examined the effect of art therapy on the cognitive performance of a multisite, ethnically diverse sample (
N = 91) of older adults. Participants were recruited from several U.S. facilities that included a community center, a retirement center, an adult daycare, an assisted living facility, and a skilled nursing facility. Cognitive training strategies served as a framework for the study's 10-week art therapy intervention protocol. A t test and a univariate linear regression indicated, with a medium effect size (
d = .064), that the art therapy treatment was associated with significantly improved cognitive performance. Other findings suggest that session duration and art therapy approach significantly correlated with improved cognitive performance. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
 (Source: journal abstract)
