T1  - Neuropsychological testing through a Nintendo Wii® console
AN  - 754054776; 2010-15322-006
AB  - In recent years, videogames have demonstrated their positive effects in the psychological treatments and cognitive training of the old population. In this paper we present a pilot study in which a group of elderly people in an old people's home was requested to play a set of cognitive tasks administered through a popular videogames console, the Nintendo Wii
®. The results obtained by comparing the Wii
® cognitive games with traditional paper and pencil tests arc described and discussed to orient further improvements. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
 (Source: journal abstract)
