T1  - Editorial
AN  - 896409401; 2011-21307-001
AB  - In this special issue of 
Educational and Child Psychology on Reasoning in Children and Adolescents, most contributions focus on how to enhance reasoning in children aged between five and twelve years. Methods of "training" children's reasoning that are described in these papers vary from very simple forms of feedback to quite extensive cognitive training programmes in the area of inductive reasoning. Some contributors study the effects of training on transfer tasks; others introduce computerized activities of various kinds. Whereas the majority of the papers in this volume focus on the effects of training or feedback on test scores, others focus more upon the reasoning process itself. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
