TY  - JOUR
T1  - Cognitive training in aging and disease (COTRAD): Does it work in Italy?
AN  - 619742175; 2002-01182-036
AB  - A survey was designed to detect the characteristics of rehabilitative approaches to cognitive deficits of aging and dementia. 39% of the treated Ss were 70-79 years old, and 22% were 80 or older; 54.5% were home dwelling and 27.3% were institutionalized. The most frequent diagnoses were aging-related cognitive decline (29.5%) and dementia (39%). Of the 10 reported therapeutic interventions, reality orientation therapy (ROT) was applied the most frequently (20.7%), followed by memory rehabilitation (17.2%). In contrast, psychomotor rehabilitation and validation therapies were the least represented (5.2%). Several professional roles were engaged, and 57.7% of the protocols require an active role of the carer. The efficacy was monitored by both clinical judgement and psychometric evaluation at the end, and 3 mo after the end of treatments. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
