TY  - JOUR
T1  - Kognitives Training: Ein Programm zur Förderung von Vorschulkindern mit intellektuellen Defiziten
TT  - Cognitive training: A program to educate pre-school children with mental deficits
AN  - 619520230; 2000-13656-002
AB  - Examined a cognitive training program to educate preschool children with mental deficits. A group of 12 preschool children (8 boys, 6 girls; aged 5–7 yrs) received 3 mos of cognitive training. Ss were then compared to a control group of 6 children (3 boys, 3 girls) that had undergone early childhood education. Prior to training a family questionnaire (FB; Familienfragebogen) was completed for both S groups. 4 scales of the questionnaire reveal findings which indicate a dysfunctional family structure. The tests administered immediately after training included: (1) the Grundintelligenztest (CFT1; Weiß & Osterland; a basic intelligence test), (2) the Kaufman Assessment Battery for Children (K-ABC; Melchers & Preuß, 1991); and (3) the Matching Familiar Figures Test (MFF; Kagan, 1964). IQ test scores for logical reasoning showed significant improvement for the test group. Testing 1 yr later revealed that the effect was still present and that it was independent from pretraining IQ and family stress. The findings and their significance as well as the validity of the testing instruments are discussed. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
